**7.2 Non-Disclosure Period**  
The obligations of confidentiality shall remain in effect for a period of five (5) years following the termination of this Agreement.

### ARTICLE VIII: FORCE MAJEURE

**8.1 Definition**  
Neither party shall be liable for any failure to perform its obligations hereunder if such failure results from events beyond its reasonable control, including but not limited to natural disasters, war, terrorism, or government action.

**8.2 Notification**  
The party affected by a force majeure event shall notify the other parties in writing within seven (7) days of the occurrence of such event.

